/**
 * Returns a debounced version of fn that only fires after
 * `delay` ms have passed without another call.
 *
 * @param {Function} fn - function to debounce
 * @param {number} delay - delay in milliseconds
 * @returns {Function} debounced function
 */
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer = null;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}
```

Uses a closure to keep the timer handle between calls and clearTimeout to cancel any pending invocation, which is the standard pattern for search-as-you-type or resize-handler use cases.

